import Nested.Inv
import ZigLean.Sep.Full.Auto
import ZigLean.Sep.Full.Tick
import ZigLean.Sep.Full.TSum

/-!
# A translated nested loop in the full-state logic

`Nested/Gen.lean` is the committed translation of `nested.zig` (retained AIR in
`air/`, checked byte for byte by `check.sh`). `pairs(acc, n)` runs an inner
`while (j < i)` loop inside the body of an outer `while (i < n)` loop; both share the locals
`pairsLocals` and the inner loop is the separate def `pairs.loop14`, called from the outer body
`pairs.loop5` as `Zig.loop (pairs.loop14 p0) pairs.again14`.

Both loops' invariants, measures and exit posts are generated by `air2lean-invgen` into
`Nested/Inv.lean` (P09, `docs/invariant-synthesis.md`) and registered with `@[fsym_inv]`; `check.sh`
regenerates them and checks that seeded mutants of them fail. The inner loop is a counted loop;
the outer loop's body runs it, and the generator reads it as its exit post, so the outer
invariant states `*acc` over the library sum `tsum` (`S2c′`). `pairs_total` is proved by `fsym`
alone: at the outer loop it applies `FTotalTriple.loop_measure` with the outer loop's definitions,
and in each run of the outer body the inner loop's.

Every body run takes a step (`Zig.tick`), so the invariants carry the plain mode (`plain`,
`docs/sep-full-state.md` §Step ticks) and `fsym` pays each step with it (`tick_plain`).

Its strength log (the legacy total triple on every `Mem.FSeqPlain` memory, the strength check of
`docs/proof-framework.md`) is `tests/roadmap/strength-log/LoopTactics.lean`.
-/

namespace Nested.Proof
open Zig Zig.Full Zig.Full.FAssn Zig.Full.Auto

/-- `pairs` adds `0 + 1 + … + (n - 1)` to `*acc`, under the premise that the sum fits; its steps
run in the plain mode. -/
theorem pairs_total (p : Ptr) (n : BitVec 32) (v : BitVec 64) (hfit : v.toNat + tsum n.toNat (fun u => u) < 2 ^ 64) :
    FTotalTriple (up (pts p 8 v) ⋆ plain) (pairs p n)
      (fun _ => up (pts p 8 (BitVec.ofNat 64 (v.toNat + tsum n.toNat (fun u => u)))) ⋆ plain) := by
  unfold pairs
  fsym

end Nested.Proof

-- Only the standard axioms: no `sorryAx`, no `native_decide` (`Lean.ofReduceBool`).
/-- info: 'Nested.Proof.pairs_total' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] -/
#guard_msgs in
#print axioms Nested.Proof.pairs_total
